  "notes": "{干|ほ}す means to dry something by exposing it to air or sun.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{乾|かわ}く→乾く：00786_kawaku⟧ (intransitive, to dry)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{洗濯物|せんたくもの}→洗濯物：09533_sentakumono⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{干|ほ}す: to hang laundry to dry\n- ⟦{布団|ふとん}→布団：01720_futon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{干|ほ}す: to air out a futon\n- {干|ほ}し⟦{物|もの}→物：02259_mono⟧: things hung out to dry\n- {干|ほ}し⟦{竿|ざお}→竿：24133_sao⟧: drying pole\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{干物|ひもの}→干物：12423_himono⟧: dried fish\n- ⟦{干|ほ}しぶどう→干しぶどう：20308_hoshibudou⟧: raisins (dried grapes)\n- ⟦{梅干|うめぼ}し→梅干し：13110_umeboshi⟧: pickled plum\n\nThe kanji {干|ほ}す relates to drying/draining.",
